.TH IMUD\-MQTT.CONF 5 "2026-07-20" "imud 1.6.2" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-mqtt.conf \- configuration file for imud-mqtt(8)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/imud/imud-mqtt.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configuration for the
.BR imud-mqtt (8)
bridge daemon, which reads imud's binary stream socket and publishes scalar
telemetry topics (plus Home Assistant discovery) to an MQTT broker.  The daemon
runs whenever
.B enabled
is true and stays healthy under systemd; it does not connect to a broker or
publish until
.B broker_enabled
is set (off by default).  The bridge
reads
.B only
this file (never
.IR imud.conf ).
The file is one
.B [imud-mqtt]
section of
.IR key " = " value
lines; strings are double-quoted and
.RB \(oq # \(cq
begins a comment.  Requires imud's
.B [stream]
output enabled.
.PP
Keys marked
.B [hot]
are reloaded on
.BR SIGHUP ;
keys marked
.B [restart]
take effect on the next service start.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [restart]
Run the MQTT bridge daemon.  With it true and
.B broker_enabled
false the daemon runs but publishes nothing; set it false to not run the bridge
at all (it exits cleanly, so systemd does not restart it).
.TP
.B broker_enabled
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Connect to the broker and publish (the bridge's only output).  This keeps a
fresh install from repeatedly dialing a broker that is not configured yet.
.TP
.B socket
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq/run/imud/imud-stream.sock\(dq )\ [restart]
imud stream socket to read.
.TP
.B broker_addr
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq127.0.0.1\(dq )\ [restart]
Broker host (name or IP).
.TP
.B broker_port
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 1883 )\ [restart]
Broker TCP port.
.TP
.B client_id
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqimud\(dq )\ [restart]
MQTT client id; also the Home Assistant device/node id.
.TP
.B keepalive_s
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 30 )\ [restart]
MQTT keepalive interval in seconds.
.TP
.B topic_prefix
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqimud\(dq )\ [restart]
Prefix for all published topics.
.TP
.B rate_hz
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 5 )\ [hot]
Publish rate in Hz.
.TP
.B qos
.RI ( int ,\ default:\ 0 )\ [hot]
Publish QoS (0, 1, or 2).
.TP
.B retain
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [hot]
Retain published values so late subscribers / Home Assistant see current state.
.TP
.B units
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqdeg\(dq )\ [hot]
.B deg
(degrees, \(de/min, m, \(deC) or
.B rad
(SI: radians, rad/s).
.TP
.B publish_heave
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [hot]
Publish the
.B environment/heave
topic.
.TP
.B ha_discovery
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ true )\ [restart]
Publish Home Assistant MQTT-discovery configs.
.TP
.B ha_prefix
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dqhomeassistant\(dq )\ [restart]
Home Assistant discovery topic prefix.
.TP
.BR username ", " password
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq )\ [restart]
Broker authentication.  A plaintext
.B password
here should be protected with restrictive file permissions.
.TP
.B tls
.RI ( bool ,\ default:\ false )\ [restart]
Enable TLS (with an empty
.B tls_cafile
the system CA store is used).
.TP
.B tls_cafile
.RI ( string ,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq )\ [restart]
CA certificate path for TLS.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-mqtt.conf
This file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud-mqtt (8),
.BR imud.conf (5),
.BR imud (8),
.BR mosquitto (8)
